<!--
  Every URL below is a real route this app serves. The home page is one
  scrolling document, so #about / #experience / #projects / #contact are
  anchors within `/` and are deliberately NOT listed as separate pages; the
  detail routes are, because they render their own page and their own <h1>.

  The domain is the real canonical, https://bhavye.vercel.app/. It is
  declared in five places that have to change together: here, index.html
  (canonical, og:url, JSON-LD), public/robots.txt, public/llms.txt and `site`
  in src/content/profile.ts.

  Every lastmod is the day the content behind that URL was last verified,
  not the day the file was touched, bumping them without a content change is
  noise a crawler learns to ignore.

  Routes come from:
    experience  src/content/experience.ts  (slug per entry)
    projects    src/content/projects/index.ts  (projectIds)
    objects     src/content/objects.ts  (slug per entry)
    library     src/content/library.ts  (/library and a slug per book)
  Adding an entry there means adding a url block here.

  The two /object/ URLs are listed because they are real routes with their own
  <h1>, their own copy and their own canonical, not because they are 3D
  props. A prop that only opened a modal would have no URL to list and must
  not be given an invented one.

  ALL of them are listed and indexable, the reserved project slot included
  (owner, 2026-09-14: "index all my website"). Each one also has a static HTML
  file of its own in the build (scripts/routePages.ts), so a crawler that does
  not run JavaScript gets that page's title, canonical and text.

  Also served at /sitemap (vite.config.ts, public/_redirects, vercel.json).
-->
